      "title": "Guide",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Guide\n\n## Models\n- Upscaler in `upscale_models/`: `4x_IllustrationJaNai_V1_DAT2_190k` (sharper, slower) or `4x_IllustrationJaNai_V1_ESRGAN_135k` (faster). Both are non-commercial (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).\n- Background removal: downloaded into `models/RMBG/` the first time a **model** is used. **RMBG-2.0** is non-commercial only; **BEN2** is free for commercial use.\n\n## How it works\n1. **Image** is upscaled 4x.\n2. **model** finds the character on the upscaled picture and cuts it out.\n3. **Result** saves a transparent PNG at 4x size in `output/nobg/`.\n\n## Settings\n- **upscale model**: see Models.\n- **model**: RMBG-2.0 · BEN2 · BEN · INSPYRENET.\n- **process res** 2048: size the model looks at (max 2048). Lower = less VRAM, rougher edges.\n- **sensitivity** 1: lower it if bits of background are left behind.\n- **mask offset** -2: negative trims the edge (removes halos and fringes), positive grows it (keeps the outer line art).\n- **mask blur** 0: 1 smooths jagged edges.\n- **refine edges**: darkens the semi-transparent edge pixels slightly. Off if the outline looks too dark.\n\n## Previews\n- Inside the subgraph, the *Previews* group keeps the upscaled picture and the mask. *Result* has the cut-out.\n\n## Inside the subgraph\n- Invert, unload model, background (Alpha or a solid colour): the *Remove background* node.\n\n## Batch\n- One picture per run. For a folder, copy it into `input/` and queue one run per picture.\n\nNeeds ComfyUI-RMBG.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
